%N A399595 Number of nonnegative integer solutions to the equation 2*x^2 + 3*y^2 = n.
%H A399595 Robert Israel, <a href="/A399595/b399595.txt">Table of n, a(n) for n = 0..10000</a>
%F A399595 G.f.: (1 + theta_3(q^2))*(1 + theta_3(q^3))/4, where theta_3() is the Jacobi theta function.
%p A399595 G:= (1+JacobiTheta3(0,q^2))*(1+JacobiTheta3(0,q^3))/4:
%p A399595 gfun:-seriestolist(series(G,q,100)); # _Robert Israel_, Sep 08 2026
%t A399595 nmax = 99; CoefficientList[Series[(1 + EllipticTheta[3, 0, q^2]) (1 + EllipticTheta[3, 0, q^3])/4, {q, 0, nmax}], q]
%Y A399595 The number of integer solutions is given by A108563.
%Y A399595 The number of positive integer solutions is given by A084863.
%Y A399595 Cf. A002480, A119395.
